What MeatSoko can adopt
1. Stronger homepage hierarchy — P1
CleanPro has a clearer service-led structure: the visitor quickly understands what the business does and what action to take.
MeatSoko should adopt:
A clear hero statement focused on buying meat/food online.
One primary CTA: Shop Meat.
Secondary CTA: Browse All Products.
Immediately below: key benefits such as Fresh • Quality • Delivered • Secure Payment.
This would reduce the current catalogue-heavy feeling.

2. Make the customer journey visually obvious — P1
Instead of immediately exposing MeatSoko's enormous category structure, introduce a simple journey:
Choose what you need → Select your product → Add to cart → Choose delivery → Pay
This is especially valuable because MeatSoko currently has a very deep category structure spanning meat, dairy, veterinary products, feeds, equipment and livestock. (MeatSoko)

3. Use benefit cards — P1
CleanPro's service-oriented presentation can translate well into MeatSoko.
For example:
Fresh & Quality Assured
Products sourced and handled to maintain quality.
Cold-Chain Delivery
Fresh products handled appropriately from source to delivery.
Secure Payments
Pay securely using supported local payment methods.
Reliable Delivery
Clear delivery areas, fees and expected delivery times.
These should contain real operational claims only—not marketing promises the business cannot substantiate.

4. Make the meat proposition visually dominant — P1
The current MeatSoko navigation gives substantial visual space to many unrelated agricultural categories. (MeatSoko)
I would introduce a prominent:
Shop Meat
section containing:
Beef
Goat & Mutton
Chicken & Poultry
Minced Meat
Offal
Meat Bundles
Then separately:
