What I would NOT adopt
❌ Don't copy the service-business model
CleanPro sells a relatively small set of services. MeatSoko is an e-commerce marketplace with products, inventory, cart, delivery and payment.
❌ Don't replace the catalogue with a marketing-heavy homepage
MeatSoko still needs strong product discovery.
❌ Don't hide all categories
The solution isn't removing the catalogue; it's progressively exposing it.
❌ Don't use generic trust claims
For meat, claims such as "100% authentic" are less useful than concrete information about freshness, handling, sourcing, packaging and delivery.

